## Summary

I implemented automatic tuning of the raft engine's `batch_compression_threshold` in TiKV's configuration validation logic, in `src/config/mod.rs`.

### Changes

**1. Added accessors to `RaftEngineConfig`** (around line 1996) so the `batch_compression_threshold` field is readable and updatable in-place:

```rust
pub fn batch_compression_threshold(&self) -> RaftEngineReadableSize {
    self.config.batch_compression_threshold
}

pub fn mut_batch_compression_threshold(&mut self) -> &mut RaftEngineReadableSize {
    &mut self.config.batch_compression_threshold
}
```

**2. Added the auto-tuning logic in the main `TikvConfig::validate`** (after `store_io_pool_size` is finalized, around line 3695):

```rust
// When async IO is enabled (i.e. `store-io-pool-size` > 0), raft logs are
// written in smaller batches, so a smaller batch compression threshold
// yields better compression. Automatically tune it to 4KB unless the user
// has explicitly overridden the raft-engine default.
if self.raft_store.store_io_pool_size > 0
    && self.raft_engine.batch_compression_threshold()
        == RawRaftEngineConfig::default().batch_compression_threshold
{
    *self.raft_engine.mut_batch_compression_threshold() = RaftEngineReadableSize::kb(4);
}
```

### Behavior against the requirements
- **Async I/O detection** — checks `store_io_pool_size > 0`.
- **Auto-tune to 4KB** — only when async I/O is on *and* the threshold still equals the raft-engine library default (8KB, sourced from `RawRaftEngineConfig::default()` rather than a hardcoded constant).
- **Preserve user values** — a non-default (user-set) threshold fails the equality check, so it is left untouched regardless of async I/O.
- **Async I/O disabled** — when `store_io_pool_size == 0`, the first condition is false, so the default threshold is left unmodified.

